{%- comment -%}
  announcement-bar — the UTILITY ROW. Pale sage strip above the header.

  Measured from the live site: ground #EEF2EE, 47.5px tall, teal type.

  It carries two things from 10/09/2026: the standing message on the left and
  the utility nav on the right. That is the whole point of the header
  restructure — the strip was 47.5px of chrome holding one sentence across
  1,500px, so the utility links move into space the header was already paying
  for, and the nav band below keeps only the product categories. Total header
  height is unchanged at 242px (47.5 + 145.5 + 1 + 49).

  THE LINKS COME FROM A MENU, NOT FROM BLOCKS. The mobile drawer lives in
  header-bottom.liquid and Liquid cannot read another section's blocks, so
  blocks here would have stripped Home, News, About Us and Contact out of the
  drawer entirely. A linklist IS readable from both sections, so one menu
  renders here on desktop and inside the drawer below 900. Set the same menu
  in both sections or the drawer will come up short.

  The message TRUNCATES rather than wraps. The links are the load-bearing
  content, and a wrapped strip grows the header, which is the exact fault this
  restructure exists to fix. Keep the text short and it will never be cut.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign util = linklists[section.settings.utility_menu]
  assign has_links = false
  if util.links.size > 0
    assign has_links = true
  endif
-%}

{%- if section.settings.text != blank or has_links -%}
  <div class="ann{% unless has_links %} ann--centred{% endunless %}">
    {%- if section.settings.text != blank -%}
      {%- if section.settings.link != blank -%}
        <a class="ann__msg" href="{{ section.settings.link }}">{{ section.settings.text }}</a>
      {%- else -%}
        <span class="ann__msg">{{ section.settings.text }}</span>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if has_links -%}
      <nav class="ann__nav" aria-label="Utility">
        {%- for link in util.links -%}
          <a class="ann__link{% if link.current %} is-active{% endif %}" href="{{ link.url }}"{% if link.current %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ link.title }}</a>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </nav>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
/* Chrome, not a content band: its own padding, full width, no max-width. */
.fye .ann {
  background: var(--sage-pale);
  color: var(--ink);
  padding-inline: var(--s7);            /* 32px, matching the header rows */
  min-height: 47.5px;                   /* measured */
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: var(--s7);
}
/* With no menu set it falls back to the old centred single message. */
.fye .ann--centred { justify-content: center; }

.fye .ann__msg {
  color: inherit;
  font-size: 12px;
  font-weight: var(--fw-light);
  letter-spacing: 0.01em;
  line-height: 1.4;
  /* min-width: 0 is load-bearing. A flex item defaults to min-width: auto —
     "at least as wide as my content" — so without it the sentence refuses to
     shrink and shoves the links off the right edge instead of ellipsing. */
  min-width: 0;
  white-space: nowrap;
  overflow: hidden;
  text-overflow: ellipsis;
}
a.ann__msg { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }

.fye .ann__nav {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: var(--s6);                       /* 24px */
  flex: 0 0 auto;                       /* the links never shrink */
}
.fye .ann__link {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  min-height: 47.5px;                   /* fills the band, so the tap target is
                                           47.5px even though the type is 11px */
  color: var(--ink);
  font-size: 11px;
  font-weight: var(--fw-medium);
  letter-spacing: 0.14em;
  line-height: 1;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  white-space: nowrap;
  text-decoration: none;
  transition: text-decoration-color var(--dur) var(--ease);
}
/* Hover is an UNDERLINE, not a colour shift, and this is a deliberate
   departure from the system's "hover goes sage green" rule. Sage green type on
   this pale sage ground measures about 2.4:1 at 11px, well under 4.5:1. The
   type stays full-strength teal and sage green moves to the rule instead. */
.fye .ann__link:hover {
  color: var(--ink);
  text-decoration: underline;
  text-decoration-color: var(--sage);
  text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
  text-underline-offset: 5px;
}
.fye .ann__link.is-active {
  text-decoration: underline;
  text-decoration-color: var(--sage-deep);
  text-decoration-thickness: 2px;
  text-underline-offset: 5px;
}
.fye .ann__link:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--teal); outline-offset: 3px; }

@media (max-width: 900px) {
  /* Below 900 the drawer owns the utility links: header-bottom renders the
     same menu inside it. The strip keeps its message and its measured height,
     centred as it was before the restructure. */
  .fye .ann { padding-inline: var(--pad-x); justify-content: center; }
  .fye .ann__nav { display: none; }
  .fye .ann__msg { font-size: 11px; }
}
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Announcement bar",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "text", "label": "Message", "default": "Ethically sourced, independently certified, fairly priced." },
    { "type": "url", "id": "link", "label": "Message link" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Utility nav" },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "The right-hand links: Home, guides, News, About us, Contact. Use a MENU, not blocks — the mobile drawer reads the same menu, so whatever you put here also lands in the drawer. Set the same menu in the Header section. Keep the message short: it truncates to protect the links." },
    { "type": "link_list", "id": "utility_menu", "label": "Utility menu" }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
